      "id": 1,
      "text": "Méier was named after Augusto Duque Estrada Meyer, who received part of the land as a gift.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scribd.com/document/922509585/History-of-Meier-by-Marcos-Neves",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The neighborhood began as an 18th‑century sugarcane farm that was split into three parcels after a dispute.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scribd.com/document/922509585/History-of-Meier-by-Marcos-Neves",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Méier’s train station opened on May 13, 1889, and the neighborhood’s founding date is celebrated as that anniversary.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.scribd.com/document/922509585/History-of-Meier-by-Marcos-Neves",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Rio Dance Center, founded in 1973, once taught actress Adriana Esteves and TV host Fátima Bernardes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%A9ier",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Shopping do Méier, one of Brazil’s first malls, opened in 1963 and still anchors the commercial heart of the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/M%C3%A9ier",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
